The stream indicator (play/stop button) was showing incorrect state in two scenarios:
1. On first load of the application
2. When switching between detector tabs

## Root Cause

The issue was in the `LiveView` component's useEffect that checks stream status via `/ViewController/getLiveViewActive`. The effect only depended on `[hostIP, hostPort]`, which meant:

- Stream status was only checked when the component mounted or host connection changed
- When switching tabs (`activeTab` changes), the stream status wasn't re-checked
- Each detector tab could have different stream states, but the UI wouldn't reflect this

## Solution

Added `activeTab` and `dispatch` to the useEffect dependency array:

```javascript
// Before
